{"name":"Alpine Morning Blue","hex":"#a6ccd8","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alpine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or inhabiting mountains, especially above the timberline.","Alternative letter-case form of Alpine: Of, relating to, or inhabiting the Alps, a large mountain range in Europe."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants, native to mountain habitats, often grown in rock gardens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alpine"},{"term":"morning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The early part of the day, especially from midnight to noon. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The early part of anything."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good morning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/500px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/1280px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/500px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Morning on a farm in Namibia, just after sunrise","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMorning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Comet_ison.jpg/500px-Comet_ison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.